  "review": {
    "en": "One June day in London: a woman prepares a party, and a former soldier unravels across the city. Woolf passes the narration from mind to mind as Big Ben strikes, and the two lives never meet yet answer each other. It is a short book that holds war, age, love and the pleasure of a fine morning.",
    "zh": "伦敦六月的一天：一个女人筹备晚会，一个退伍士兵在城市另一端逐渐崩溃。大本钟报时之间，伍尔夫让叙述从一颗心灵传到另一颗；两人从未相遇，却彼此呼应。这本薄书装下了战争、衰老、爱，以及一个晴朗早晨的愉悦。"
